course: dictionary
lesson: 2908
title: Downstream
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Downstream means in the direction a river or stream flows, towards the sea. Water always moves from the hills, where a river starts, towards the sea, so downstream is the way the water is going.
explain: «Water under a calm surface can still be moving fast enough to pull a swimmer downstream.» The surface may look still, but the water underneath is moving, and it carries the swimmer along. Check it: swap in "along with the flow of the river" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Downstream can also describe a place. «Further downstream» means a spot further along the river, nearer the sea. Its opposite is upstream, which means back towards where the river starts.
fact: Downstream means in the direction a river flows, towards the sea.
fact: Upstream is the opposite: back towards where the river starts in the hills.
fact: «Float downstream» means to drift along with the water.
fact: Beaver dams slow rivers down, so they can reduce flooding downstream: places further along the river stay drier.
fact: Beavers are called ecosystem engineers because they change the land around them more than almost any animal but people do.
exercise: «The boat was carried downstream by the strong current.» Which way did the boat go? | Across the river to the other bank | Back up towards the hills | Round in a circle on the spot | *Towards the sea, with the flow of the river
exercise: «Further downstream» means a place that is? | *Further along the river, towards the sea | Under a bridge only | Nearer to where the river starts in the hills | Dry, with no water at all
exercise: Which word is the opposite of downstream? | Sideways | *Upstream | Downhill | Underwater
test: «To swim against the current» means to swim which way? | Along the bank | Under the water | *Upstream | Downstream
test: «Beaver dams reduce flooding downstream.» Which places get less flooding? | Places up in the hills where the river starts | *Places further along the river, towards the sea | Only the dam itself | Places that were never near the river
exam: Which sentence uses downstream correctly? | The leaf floated downstream, back up to the spring in the hills | The leaf floated downstream, so it rolled up the hill | The leaf downstream was loud and sad | *The leaf floated downstream and out to sea
